V4L2 UAPI headers

linux/videodev2.h, linux/v4l2-controls.h and linux/v4l2-common.h are verbatim
copies from Linux 6.12 (include/uapi/linux). Each carries
"(GPL-2.0+ WITH Linux-syscall-note) OR BSD-3-Clause" and is used here under
the BSD-3-Clause option.

linux/media.h is a GENERATED file (BSD-3-Clause): uapi/media.spec holds the interface facts (names,
member types and order, values, ioctl numbers) and tools/gen-media-h.py writes the header from it. It was
rewritten on 2026-10-08 after docs/AUDIT.md (F-01) found the earlier file to be a trimmed copy of Linux's
GPL-2.0-only media.h. The names, member order and values are interface facts and necessarily equal Linux's;
the text, constant notation, grouping and comments are our own (no #define line is identical to Linux's).
The rewrite was done by an AI session from a mechanically extracted fact sheet, not in a legal clean room;
the model may have seen the Linux text in training. tests/abi/media_facts_check.py checks the header against
tests/abi/media-facts.txt, and gen_abi.py compares it with a Linux tree.

linux/v4l2-subdev.h, linux/v4l2-mediabus.h and linux/media-bus-format.h are
GPL-2.0 only and are deliberately NOT copied; the same replacement is still to
be done for them (open question Q1 in docs/specs/SPEC_media_v4l2_native.md in
bzdOS/bsdOS).
